From 128b305a394b415fbbc5fbee392064560d82fd74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JoshuaHayesWasHere <josh.hayes121@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:40:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): the jstack tree keeps to one weight, a crew task's
 mark is a ring by thirds and a scout's a diamond, and sky marks only live
 work

Every name in the tree is 13/400 and every word beside it 11/400: a root's name drops its 500.
Levels step by ink and height: a root row 32px at full ink with 24px above it, a home 28px at
80%, a worker 26px at 60%, a home's counts at 80%.

A crew task's three segments are one 8px ring filled by thirds, crew, review and merge, and
empty while queued. A scout's mark is a 10px diamond: hollow while queued, its lower half filled
while it scouts, filled once its report is in, and its word says which.

One accent, sky (#0369a1 light, #38bdf8 dark), marks live work only: a ring or diamond at work,
and the badge of a root with live work under it. Live is a launched task not asking you, not
quiet, stalled or held, and not a scout whose report is in; it is read whatever the attention
setting shows. Amber (#b45309, #fbbf24) marks what asks you. Every other mark and badge is
neutral at 60% ink, muted while queued, and text stays neutral. A live row says "live" to a
screen reader, and a live root "live work inside".

The server reads each scout from its row of jbus's work.json and its `scout` (queued, scouting
or report in), in place of scouts.json, which jbus no longer writes; a scout's title is read
from its request in the home's scouts folder. A task in the contract is a crew task, with its
stage and pull request, or a scout, with where it stands.
